From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Opsero <noreply@opsero.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:43:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: xilinx: isppipeline: fix gamma LUT plane order

The ISP pipeline core (xlnx,isppipeline-1.0, the Vitis Vision
ISPPipeline_accel) exposes its gamma tables as a single 768-byte
gamma_lut memory at 0x800-0xbff. The core's gammacorrection stage
applies table k (bytes 256*k .. 256*k+255) to plane k of its internal
pixel, and that pixel is packed B, G, R from the least significant
byte up (the demosaic stage writes b to bits 7:0, g to 15:8 and r to
23:16). The per-plane tables are therefore:

  0x800  blue
  0x900  green
  0xa00  red

The driver writes the red table to 0x800, the blue table to 0x900 and
the green table to 0xa00, so red_gamma acts on blue, green_gamma on red
and blue_gamma on green. Fix the offsets to match the core.

With the offsets fixed the default curves must also be equal: the
defaults were red 2.0, green 1.5, blue 2.0, which after the offset
fix would give every picture a green tint, and before it gave a
magenta tint (the green curve landed on red). Use 2.0 for green as
well: it is the value the driver already uses for red, blue and the
mono gamma control, so the default output is colour neutral and the
overall tone curve is unchanged for the two channels that were
already at 2.0.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Opsero <noreply@opsero.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-isppipeline.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-isppipeline.c b/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-isppipeline.c
index e07aee7..ffc8a10 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-isppipeline.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-isppipeline.c
@@ -162,9 +162,13 @@
 #define XISP_RGAIN_REG			(0x30)
 #define XISP_BGAIN_REG			(0x38)
 #define XISP_PAWB_REG			(0x54)
-#define XISP_GAMMA_RED_REG		(0x800)
-#define XISP_GAMMA_BLUE_REG		(0x900)
-#define XISP_GAMMA_GREEN_REG		(0xA00)
+/*
+ * The gamma_lut memory holds one 256-entry table per plane, in the
+ * B, G, R plane order of the core's internal pixel format.
+ */
+#define XISP_GAMMA_BLUE_REG		(0x800)
+#define XISP_GAMMA_GREEN_REG		(0x900)
+#define XISP_GAMMA_RED_REG		(0xA00)
 
 #define XISP_MAX_HEIGHT			(4320)
 #define XISP_MAX_WIDTH			(8192)
@@ -222,7 +226,7 @@
 #define XISP_RED_GAMMA_MAX			(40)
 #define XISP_RED_GAMMA_DEFALUT			(20)
 #define XISP_GREEN_GAMMA_MAX			(40)
-#define XISP_GREEN_GAMMA_DEFALUT		(15)
+#define XISP_GREEN_GAMMA_DEFALUT		(20)
 #define XISP_BLUE_GAMMA_MAX			(40)
 #define XISP_BLUE_GAMMA_DEFALUT			(20)
 #define XISP_HDR_ALPHA_MAX			(256)
